        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "CDIAL lists Hindi ṭhaṇḍā, \"cold\", under a reconstructed ṭhaṇḍha, which it sets under Sanskrit stabdha, \"stiff, solidified\", tracing the sense from \"firm\" through \"sluggish\" to \"cold\" (CDIAL 13676); it gives no Marwari form. DEDR compares Dravidian words for \"cool\", such as Tamil taṇ (DEDR 3045)."
            }
          ]
        },
